          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most homeowners, the Scotts Elite is the broadcast spreader to buy: its dual rotors give a wider, more even pattern, EdgeGuard keeps product off hard surfaces, and the settings are on the bag. On a budget or a smaller lawn, the EdgeGuard DLX or Mini do the same job with fewer extras. If you want a spreader that lasts a decade or you have a large lawn, the stainless LESCO 101186 is worth its premium, and the Earthway 2150 gets you most of the way there for less.
          </p>
